# Trivy ignore list — HIGH/CRITICAL CVEs we accept on the published images.
#
# Format: one CVE/GHSA per line, optional comment after. Trivy reads this
# at the repo root automatically (also passed explicitly to the scan
# action in .github/workflows/docker-scan.yml).
#
# Policy:
#  - We never ignore CVEs in code Diluxite executes against untrusted
#    input (HTTP bodies, MCP tool args, markdown content, etc.).
#  - We DO ignore CVEs that exist only in build-tool vendored deps that
#    never run on user data — typically `pnpm`'s bundled copies of
#    `minimatch`, `tar`, `picomatch`, etc. pnpm only ever processes our
#    own `package.json` and the controlled lockfile, never user input.
#
# Each ignore is paired with a tracking note. When the bundled pnpm
# updates these libs, we drop the entry.

# === pnpm bundled deps (corepack-installed pnpm@10.27.0) ===
# These live under /usr/local/lib/node_modules/corepack/* and only execute
# during `pnpm exec` on our own controlled inputs. Drop these when the
# pnpm vendored bundle refreshes upstream.

# minimatch <10.2.x in the pnpm bundle — RegEx-based DoS via crafted patterns.
# Our pnpm only globs files in apps/api/node_modules; no user-controlled input.
CVE-2026-26996
CVE-2026-27903
CVE-2026-27904

# picomatch <4.0.4 in the pnpm bundle — same DoS class.
CVE-2026-33671

# node-tar <7.5.11 in the pnpm bundle — file-overwrite/path-traversal via
# crafted archives. pnpm never extracts user-supplied tarballs in our flow.
CVE-2026-23745
CVE-2026-23950
CVE-2026-24842
CVE-2026-26960
CVE-2026-29786
CVE-2026-31802

# === TODO for v1.0.0-alpha.8 ===
# Refactor runtime to not need pnpm at all (invoke `node --import tsx src/index.ts`
# directly), then `rm -rf` corepack from the runtime image. That eliminates the
# pnpm vendored bundle from the published images and we drop this file.
